<span class="kicker">2026-07-16 / RIDGEWELL GUIDES</span><h1>How Much Does It Cost to Resurface a Driveway or Patio</h1>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section article-section"><div class="wrap editorial-layout"><article class="prose blog-content"><p>Resurfacing a driveway or patio is almost always more affordable than a full replacement, but the exact cost depends on your surface material, its current condition, and the size of the area. There’s no single number that applies to every project, since a concrete overlay and a stone repolish involve different work, but understanding what drives the price helps you know what to expect before getting quotes.</p>
<p>At<a href="/about/"> Ridgewell Landscape and Design</a>, we handle resurfacing projects across the Denver area, including Broomfield, Parker, and surrounding communities. Here’s what actually goes into the cost, and how to know if resurfacing is even the right fit for your space.</p>
<table><tbody><tr><td><b>Question</b></td><td><b>Answer</b></td></tr><tr><td>Is resurfacing cheaper than replacement?</td><td>Yes, in most cases</td></tr><tr><td>What affects the price most?</td><td>Material type, surface condition, and square footage</td></tr><tr><td>Best candidate for resurfacing?</td><td>Surfaces that are worn or fading but structurally sound</td></tr><tr><td>When is replacement the better call?</td><td>Major cracking, shifting, or base failure</td></tr></tbody></table><h2><b>What “Resurfacing” Actually Involves</b></h2>
<p>Resurfacing isn’t one single process, it depends on what material you’re working with.</p>
<p>For concrete, resurfacing typically means applying an overlay coating over the existing slab. This restores the look of the surface and covers minor imperfections without tearing out and repouring the whole driveway or patio.</p>
<p>For stone and pavers, resurfacing usually means repolishing or resealing the existing surface. Instead of an overlay, this process cleans, restores, and protects the stone itself, bringing back its original color and finish. If your pavers need routine upkeep rather than a full resurface, our guide on<a href="/blog/how-to-clean-a-paver-patio/"> how to clean a paver patio</a> covers the simpler maintenance steps.</p>
<p>Both approaches work with what’s already there, which is exactly why resurfacing tends to cost less than starting over.</p>

<h2>Turn Your dream landscape a reality</h2>

